    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a potent offensive outlook, anchored by the elite 80.18 projection for **Yordan Alvarez**, who faces a favorable matchup against Englert. **Alvarez** remains the premier play, bolstered by his elite xwOBA of .479 and a solid matchup. Following closely in the \"Strong\" category are **Junior Caminero** (75.15) and **Trea Turner** (74.00). **Turner** is particularly well-positioned; despite the high-speed threat against an elite hold pitcher, his lead-off spot against Avila (5.01 xERA) provides a massive efficiency boost, making him a cornerstone for our stolen base production. Furthermore, **Lars Nootbaar** (67.77) and **Caleb Durbin** (65.51) represent exceptional secondary options against exploitable arms, with **Nootbaar** benefiting from significant positive adjustments due to the matchup against Assad.\n\nWhile our starting lineup is robust, the decision to bench **Luke Raley** (57.71) was the most difficult. **Raley**\u2019s projected efficiency was suppressed by a poor park factor and a matchup against Yesavage, leaving him just short of the threshold required to displace starters like **Dillon Dingler** or **Kazuma Okamoto**. We are monitoring the risk profile of **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.37); while he offers high-upside speed against Liberatore, the dynamic platoon penalty for left-on-left matchups is significant. Additionally, we are tracking the slow delivery of Rocker, which grants a slight efficiency bump to **Dillon Dingler** and **Colt Keith**\u2014a vital detail in our pursuit of stolen bases today. We remain cautious with **Christian Yelich**, as his platoon disadvantage against Rodriguez slightly offsets the efficiency gains from his top-of-the-order positioning.",
